# KARLHEINZ STOCKHAUSEN / STUDIE II (1954)
# syNo realization of the 380-event score data in Georg Hajdu's Max example.
# Source: Max 9 / Examples / synths / very-special-guest / stockhausen-studie-II.maxpat.
# Real-time version: Georg Hajdu. Assistance: Les Stuck, Sven Bey, Thorsten Floth,
# Catrin Groth, Ulrike Luttmann. Special thanks: Werner Funk.
# Score copyright: 1954 Stockhausen Verlag. The supplied Max example states Used with permission.
# That credit is retained; score data are NOT relicensed under syNo's 0BSD code license.
# No Max UI, image assets, or Max DSP source are bundled.
# See docs/hajdu-studie-ii.md for the translation and its sonic differences.
# Exact row order, roots, mixture types, dB endpoints and rounded-ms timing are retained.
# syNo uses e0090 edge fades, standard equal-power panning and convolution r4;
# it does NOT contain yafr2, nor claim sample-identical sound to Max.
# One common r4v3 output chain; the two After Studies remain separate pieces.
# Loop OFF. Each line below is one mixture, independent from the next onset.
# ma / mb / mc / md / me = mixture spacing 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5.
# Call arguments: root Hz, first linear intensity, last linear intensity, gate seconds.
# * opens the next argument; *2 reuses argument 2; apostrophe * takes gate from an argument.
!sc
!vt

# One reusable relative lattice; each mixture supplies its own root.
u[0 111.45254855 222.90509711 334.35764566 445.81019422 557.26274277 668.71529133 780.16783988 891.62038844 1003.072937 1114.5254855 1225.9780341 1337.4305827 1448.8831312 1560.3356798 1671.7882283 1783.2407769 1894.6933254 2006.145874 2117.5984225 2229.0509711]:5/1

# MIXTURE 1 / f[j] = root * 5^(j*1/25), j=0..4.
ma=(
 o*
 s[n1]v*>*e0090'*p-1
 s[n2]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-1
 s[n3]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-1
 s[n4]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-1
 s[n5]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-1
)

# MIXTURE 2 / f[j] = root * 5^(j*2/25), j=0..4.
mb=(
 o*
 s[n1]v*>*e0090'*p-0.5
 s[n3]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-0.5
 s[n5]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-0.5
 s[n7]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-0.5
 s[n9]v*2>*3e0090'*4p-0.5
)

# MIXTURE 3 / f[j] = root * 5^(j*3/25), j=0..4.
mc=(
 o*
 s[n1]v*>*e0090'*p0
 s[n4]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0
 s[n7]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0
 s[n10]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0
 s[n13]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0
)

# MIXTURE 4 / f[j] = root * 5^(j*4/25), j=0..4.
md=(
 o*
 s[n1]v*>*e0090'*p0.5
 s[n5]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0.5
 s[n9]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0.5
 s[n13]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0.5
 s[n17]v*2>*3e0090'*4p0.5
)

# MIXTURE 5 / f[j] = root * 5^(j*5/25), j=0..4.
me=(
 o*
 s[n1]v*>*e0090'*p1
 s[n6]v*2>*3e0090'*4p1
 s[n11]v*2>*3e0090'*4p1
 s[n16]v*2>*3e0090'*4p1
 s[n21]v*2>*3e0090'*4p1
)

